  "title": "இரவச்சம்",
  "heading": "2.31",
  "poet": "பல புலவர்கள்",
  "tinai": "unknown",
  "sangamTamil": "இன்னா இயைக இனிய ஒழிகென்று\nதன்னையே தானிரப்பத் தீர்வதற் - கென்னைகொல்\nகாதல் கவற்றும் மனத்தினாற் கண்பாழ்பட்டு\nஏதி லவரை இரவு.",
  "urai": null,
  "english": "Contentment better than mendicancy. When a man himself, begs of himself, saying, ‘Let troubles come, let joys depart!' the sting of poverty is extracted; why then, for this purpose, should any one, his mind agitated with desire, and his eye wasted with weeping, beg of strangers ?",
